SOUND
- Score and foley are made in code (audio.py). The foley (splashes, wingbeats, drips, distant calls, a
  record scratch, a slide whistle, wind and water) is synthesised.
- Drums: "MuldjordKit" by Lars Muldjord (drumgizmo.org), FreePats version, licensed under CC BY 4.0
  (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
- Samples (CC0): FreePats project (freepats.zenvoid.org) — kalimba; Karoryfer Samples / sfzinstruments — bass;
  VS Chamber Orchestra: Community Edition (Versilian Studios) — violins, cellos, log drum, bass drum;
  Versilian Community Sample Library (Versilian Studios) — marimba, vibraphone, glockenspiel, hand chimes,
  harp, woodblock, claps, shaker, conga, cajon.
  Fetch with: sh tools/fetch.sh instruments vcsl; vsco2ce; freepats; karoryfer.

BEHAVIOUR
- No numbers or claims appear on screen. What the flamingos do follows real birds: group marching and
  head-flagging displays, a running start across the water to take off, flight with neck and legs stretched
  out. The young bird's shorter, straighter bill and downy outline are a character design, not a field guide.
